        /// `expired_token_treated_as_none_then_401_path_engages`, which
        /// asserted the opposite on this exact fixture: an unauthenticated
        /// first PUT, a 401 by construction, a `force_refresh()`, and a second
        /// PUT. That was never an early refresh — it was a self-inflicted
        /// round trip once per token lifetime, and when the sidecar had not yet
        /// written the replacement the second attempt 401'd too and the whole
        /// call died terminal.
        ///
        /// The `.expect(1)` on the single route IS the assertion: no
        /// unauthenticated route exists, so a regression shows up as both a
        /// failed count and a wiremock 404.
        #[tokio::test]
